cluster-glyph-placement

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Place forced-width glyphs at the cell their cluster starts in, as Ghostty does, so a ligature spans the cells it replaces and combining marks stay on their base.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream GPUI or herdr-app places forced-width glyphs by cluster rather than by glyph index.
